{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5323) to implement `cmd/mkdir` basic directory creation in the go-unix-utils project. The task requires creating two files: `cmd/mkdir/main.go` and `cmd/mkdir/mkdir_test.go`. The scope is limited to srd034 requirements R1.1-R1.4 only (basic directory creation, error handling, --verbose flag, --help/--version flags). The -p (parents) and -m (mode) flags are explicitly NOT in scope for this task. The implementation must follow GNU coreutils behavior and be verified via differential testing against `gmkdir`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `mkdir` coreutils utility\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against Homebrew GNU reference binary (`gmkdir`)\n   - SIGPIPE handler protocol: all cmd/ utilities must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` framework for side-by-side binary comparison\n   - `DiffTest` struct with fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n   - Use `os.Mkdir` (not `os.MkdirAll`) for basic directory creation (D3)\n   - GNU-format error messages: `mkdir: cannot create directory 'NAME': REASON` (D4)\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gmkdir\")` with `t.Skip` if not found\n   - Both binaries in RunDiffTests run in the SAME WorkDir (important consideration for filesystem-modifying utilities)\n   - `buildEnv` sets `LC_ALL=C` by default in test environment\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd034-mkdir.yaml` (READ)\n     - Full SRD for mkdir with R1 (basic creation), R2 (parent -p), R3 (mode -m), R4 (differential testing)\n     - This task only implements R1.1-R1.4\n     - R1.1: Create single 