{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MzwdeQRceVULhhLmACsno4","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have a comprehensive picture. Let me compile a complete report for you.\n\n## Summary of Existing Implementation Patterns\n\nBased on my exploration of the go-unix-utils codebase, here are the key patterns I found:\n\n### 1. **cmd/ln/main.go** (Filesystem-modifying utility)\n**Full Content:**\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\nconst helpText = `Usage: ln [OPTION]... TARGET LINK_NAME\n  or:  ln [OPTION]... TARGET\n  or:  ln [OPTION]... TARGET... DIRECTORY\nIn the 1st form, create a link to TARGET with the name LINK_NAME.\nIn the 2nd form, create a link to TARGET in the current directory.\nIn the 3rd form, create links to each TARGET in DIRECTORY.\n\n  -s, --symbolic  make symbolic links instead of hard links\n      --help      display this help and exit\n      --version   output version information and exit\n`\n\nconst versionText = `ln (go-unix-utils) dev\n`\n\ntype options struct {\n\tsymbolic bool\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n\topts, targets, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ln: %s\\n\", err)\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'ln --help' for more information.\\n\")\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\tos.Exit(run(opts, targets))\n}\n\nfunc run(opts options, targets []string) int {\n\texitCode := 0\n\tlast := targets[len(targets)-1]\n\n\tswitch {\n\tcase len(targets) == 1:\n\t\tlinkName := filepath.Base(targets[0])\n\t\tif err := createLink(targets[0], linkName, opts); err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ln: %s\\n\", err)\n\t\t\texitCode = 1\n\t\t}\n\tcase isDirectory(last):\n\t\tfor _, target := range targets[:len(targets)-1] {\n\t\t\tlinkName := filepath.Join(last, filepath.Base(target))\n\t\t\tif err := createLink(target, linkName, opts); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ln: %s\\n\", err)\n\t\t\t\texitCode = 1\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\tcase len(targets) == 2:\n\t\tif err := createLink(targets[0], targets[1], opts); err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ln: %s\\n\", err)\n\t\t\texitCode = 1\n\t\t}\n\tdefault:\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ln: target '%s' is not a directory\\n\", last)\n\t\texitCode = 1\n\t}\n\n\treturn exitCode\n}\n\nfunc createLink(target, linkName string, opts options) error {\n\tif opts.symbolic {\n\t\tif err := os.Symlink(target, linkName); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to create symbolic link '%s': %s\",\n\t\t\t\tlinkName, sysError(err))\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\treturn createHardLink(target, linkName)\n}\n\nfunc createHardLink(target, linkName string) error {\n\tfi, err := os.Stat(target)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to access '%s': %s\", target, sysError(err))\n\t}\n\tif fi.IsDir() {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"'%s': hard link not allowed for directory\", target)\n\t}\n\tif err := os.Link(target, linkName); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to create hard link '%s': %s\",\n\t\t\tlinkName, sysError(err))\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc isDirectory(path string) bool {\n\tfi, err := os.Stat(path)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\treturn fi.IsDir()\n}\n\nfunc sysError(err error) string {\n\tfor u := errors.Unwrap(err); u != nil; u = errors.Unwrap(err) {\n\t\terr = u\n\t}\n\treturn err.Error()\n}\n\nfunc parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string, error) {\n\tvar opts options\n\tvar targets []string\n\n\ti := 0\n\tfor i < len(args) {\n\t\targ := args[i]\n\t\tif arg == \"--\" {\n\t\t\ttargets = append(targets, args[i+1:]...)\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\") {\n\t\t\tn, err := parseLongFlag(arg, &opts)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn opts, nil, err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ti += n\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif len(arg) > 1 && arg[0] == '-' {\n\t\t\tif err := parseShortFlags(arg[1:], &opts); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn opts, nil, err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ti++\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\ttargets = append(targets, arg)\n\t\ti++\n\t}\n\n\tif len(targets) == 0 {\n\t\treturn opts, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"missing file operand\")\n\t}\n\n\treturn opts, targets, nil\n}\n\nfunc parseLongFlag(flag string, opts *options) (int, error) {\n\tswitch flag {\n\tcase \"--help\":\n\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t\treturn 0, nil\n\tcase \"--version\":\n\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t\treturn 0, nil\n\tcase \"--symbolic\":\n\t\topts.symbolic = true\n\t\treturn 1, nil\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"unrecognized option '%s'\", flag)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc parseShortFlags(flags string, opts *options) error {\n\tfor j := 0; j < len(flags); j++ {\n\t\tswitch flags[j] {\n\t\tcase 's':\n\t\t\topts.symbolic = true\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"invalid option -- '%c'\", flags[j])\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n```\n\n**Key Patterns:**\n- Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at the start of main()\n- Has `helpText` and `versionText` constants\n- Error messages use the utility name prefix (e.g., \"ln: %s\")\n- Structured as: parseArgs → run → domain functions\n- Options are a simple struct\n- Uses an internal `sysError()` function to unwrap nested errors\n\n---\n\n### 2. **cmd/tee/main.go** (Complex I/O utility with differential testing)\n**Full Content:** (See above - 154 lines)\n\n**Key Patterns:**\n- Signal handling with `signal.Ignore(syscall.SIGPIPE)`\n- Flag parsing handles `-` for stdin passthrough\n- Named writer struct for tracking multiple outputs\n- Error handling preserves file context in stderr messages\n- Uses `errors.AsType` for error assertion pattern\n\n---\n\n### 3. **cmd/basename/main.go** (Simpler utility without filesystem modification)\n**Full Content:** (See above - 191 lines)\n\n**Key Patterns:**\n- Also calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n- Option struct includes string field (suffix)\n- Args parsing handles positional + flag combinations\n- Supports both short and long flag forms with arguments (e.g., `-s FILE` and `--suffix=FILE`)\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Testing Framework: cmd/tee/tee_test.go** (530 lines)\n**Key Patterns:**\n- Uses differential testing: compares go implementation against reference binary (gtee)\n- `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles the current package\n- `testutils.RunDiffTests()` executes test cases against both binaries\n- `testutils.NormalizeFunc` allows normalizing stdout/stderr before comparison\n- Can check file creation with `ExpectedFiles` map\n- Tests run in `t.TempDir()` for isolation\n- Comprehensive error cases: file I/O errors, broken pipes, signal handling\n\n**Test Helper Patterns:**\n- `runCapture()` - capture stdout/stderr and exit code\n- `runWithBrokenStdout()` - test SIGPIPE handling\n- `runSIGINTTest()` - test signal handling during I/O\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Testing Framework: cmd/basename/basename_test.go** (132 lines)\n**Key Patterns:**\n- Uses same `testutils.RunDiffTests()` harness\n- Can normalize binary name references in error messages\n- Discard stdout for help/version (since text differs between implementations)\n- Tests both success and error cases with exit codes\n- Tests flag combinations and edge cases\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Shared Testing Utilities: pkg/testutils/**\n\n**difftest.go** (241 lines):\n- `DiffTest` struct: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n- `RunDiffTests()` - main entry point, runs subtests comparing Go vs reference binary\n- Environment includes `LC_ALL=C` by default\n- Timeout: 10 seconds per test\n- Error output shows side-by-side divergence format\n\n**build.go** (39 lines):\n- `BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string` - compiles package to temp directory\n- Returns binary path, fatal on compile failure\n\n**Special Features:**